      "text": "Super Micro Computer, Inc.",
      "text_sha256": "8c7a91cc34506ccf402aaa2dc0c6a196a018c2dcc17716f8fec45bab4ffbb4ed",
      "title": null,
      "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1375365/000137536526000022/smci-20260630.htm"
    },
    {
      "corpus": "web",
      "coverage": "captured_document",
      "end_char": 112398,
      "passage_id": "source-2:p308",
      "published_at": null,
      "publisher": "www.sec.gov",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-09-07T21:47:14.143790+00:00",
      "source_id": "source-2",
      "start_char": 111813,
      "text": "We were incorporated in California in September 1993 and subsequently reincorporated in Delaware in March 2007. Our common stock is listed on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the symbol “SMCI”. Our 7.00% Series A Mandatory Convertible Preferred Stock (the “Mandatory Convertible Preferred Stock”) in the form of depositary shares are listed on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the ticker “SMCIP”. Our principal executive offices are located at 980 Rock Avenue, San Jose, California 95131. Our telephone number is (408) 503-8000, and our website address is www.supermicro.com.",
      "text_sha256": "d2386c07f325e3dfe85e0eb1a0d3f3256df113eb4ef99b7d53a2f423309eb21d",
      "title": null,
      "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1375365/000137536526000022/smci-20260630.htm"
    },
    {
      "corpus": "web",
      "coverage": "captured_document",
      "end_char": 247731,
      "passage_id": "source-2:p654",
      "published_at": null,
      "publisher": "www.sec.gov",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-09-07T21:47:14.143790+00:00",
      "source_id": "source-2",
      "start_char": 247378,
      "text": "Our common stock is traded on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the symbol SMCI. Public trading of our common stock began on March 29, 2007. Prior to that, there was no public market for our common stock. Our Mandatory Convertible Preferred Stock in the form of depositary shares are listed on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the symbol SMCIP.",
      "text_sha256": "aacb108b857f24441249a28af1244cb1ab93ad5b6ff2a78b846ed477850f856c",
      "title": null,
      "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1375365/000137536526000022/smci-20260630.htm"
    },
    {
      "corpus": "web",
      "coverage": "captured_document",
      "end_char": 1231,
      "passage_id": "source-3:p26",
      "published_at": null,
      "publisher": "markets.financialcontent.com",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-09-07T21:49:44.065250+00:00",
      "source_id": "source-3",
      "start_char": 531,
      "text": "In a pivotal turn of events for the AI infrastructure sector, Super Micro Computer (Nasdaq: SMCI) has successfully averted a catastrophic delisting from the Nasdaq exchange by filing its long-overdue financial reports. As of January 27, 2026, the company is back in full regulatory compliance, marking the end of a tumultuous eighteen-month period characterized by auditor resignations, internal probes, and intense federal scrutiny. While the filing brings much-needed legal stability, the immediate market reaction has been defined by sharp volatility as investors grapple with the company’s severely compressed profit margins and the \"governance discount\" that continues to weigh on its valuation.",
      "text_sha256": "2031da9b69883a8ad849c8ab5f089706f93e6c2497e3bbaac37926207abac72e",
      "title": null,
      "url": "https://markets.financialcontent.com/stocks/article/marketminute-2026-1-27-super-micro-computer-smci-regains-nasdaq-compliance-after-high-stakes-accounting-saga-igniting-fresh-market-volatility"
    },
    {
      "corpus": "web",
      "coverage": "captured_document",
      "end_char": 3355,
      "passage_id": "source-3:p30",
      "published_at": null,
      "publisher": "markets.financialcontent.com",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-09-07T21:49:44.065250+00:00",
      "source_id": "source-3",
      "start_char": 2648,
      "text": "Following the resignation, the company teetered on the brink of delisting, a move that would have forced it into the \"pink sheets\" and likely triggered a massive institutional sell-off. However, a series of strategic pivots saved the listing. In November 2024, SMCI hired BDO USA as its new independent auditor and submitted a comprehensive compliance plan to Nasdaq. By December, an internal committee completed a probe that found no evidence of misconduct but recommended a leadership shake-up, including the appointment of a new Chief Financial Officer. After receiving a final extension, the company finally delivered its audited financials on February 25, 2025, officially closing the delisting threat.",
      "text_sha256": "9a6aebe85c281e732c8122f72802d403f8bdf3c1b61b05f958529524fa4b2f59",
      "title": null,
      "url": "https://markets.financialcontent.com/stocks/article/marketminute-2026-1-27-super-micro-computer-smci-regains-nasdaq-compliance-after-high-stakes-accounting-saga-igniting-fresh-market-volatility"
    }
  ],
